  "definition": "Pointing accuracy describes how closely a spacecraft axis or payload line of sight meets its required direction or target under a declared metric. A useful value states what is being compared, the reference frame and target, the operational interval, axes or boresight, statistic and confidence. An angular number labelled only `accuracy` cannot distinguish knowledge, control or achieved end-to-end performance.[^1][^2]",
